            type: 'paragraph',
            text: 'The East German trajectory raises a different transfer problem. The FES collection describes a founding programme centered on dismantling concentrated political power and building democratic, ecological-social-market institutions, while Fischer records a distinctive social base rooted largely in church and professional networks rather than the industrial working class and documents disagreements over the pace and form of unity. The case therefore broadens the history of social democracy without proving that one programme could have been implemented unchanged across the two German states.',
