            text: 'Nepal’s 1990–2008 constitutional-monarchy sequence supplies a South Asian case of democratic restoration, royal intervention and republican abolition. The 1990 Constitution combined popular sovereignty, a Hindu constitutional monarchy, multiparty parliamentary government, ministerial responsibility, adult franchise and elected chambers, while retaining royal appointment, advice and dissolution powers. Manandhar, Malagodi and Parajulee interpret the subsequent period differently but converge on a contested transition in which party conflict, Maoist insurgency, constitutional nationalism and King Gyanendra’s direct rule strained the settlement before the 2006 movement and the 2008 abolition. This is a dated sequence, not a score for Nepal or a verdict on all Nepali communities.',
            citations: citations([], ['nepalConstitution1990', 'manandharNepalMonarchy2014', 'malagodiNepalMonarchy2011', 'parajuleeNepalHybrid2010']),
