      'Collate Law XII/1867 in the Hungarian and German originals against the French MJP transcription, the Austrian December Constitution and the full financial, military and delegations arrangements. Check the legal editions, parliamentary debates, royal assent, common-ministry practice and Hungarian constitutional scholarship before treating the compromise as a complete account of the Dual Monarchy or its nationalities.',
      'Read Pap’s complete Hungarian study and its electoral tables, then compare the 1865–1868 parliamentary cycle with later franchise laws, party organization, local political networks, women’s and minority participation, and Hungarian-language scholarship. The repository abstract sharpens the evidence gap but does not establish turnout, representation or party competition across the whole period.',
