            text: 'A Portuguese-language study by Costa, Zangelmi and Schiavo adds a participant-level caution to this Brazilian cluster. Its abstract recognizes that some CEB participants became active in unions, parties, neighborhood associations and social movements, but emphasizes less-activist perspectives and a possible gap between pastoral or Catholic-intellectual intentions and everyday local responses. This is an abstract-level anthropological interpretation, not a national survey or proof that CEBs were politically inactive; it supports keeping religious practice, political learning, organization and measured outcomes as separate evidence layers.',
            citations: citations([], ['costaZangelmiSchiavoCebs2011Portuguese', 'krischkeBrazilCEBDemocracy1991', 'meirellesCebsBaixadaFluminense2024']),
