            role: 'Haitian president whose administration operated within the occupation’s treaty and financial framework after his election in August 1915.',
            caveat: 'The U.S. institutional account describes intense external pressure and contested legitimacy; it does not establish Dartiguenave’s complete intentions, Haitian public opinion or the agency of every official who worked within the occupation.',
